   "text": "Matrix multiplication on a GPU is fast because GPUs are designed to perform parallel operations efficiently. GPUs have a large number of processing units (cores) that can execute instructions simultaneously, allowing them to perform many matrix multiplications in parallel. This parallelism is achieved through a technique called parallel processing, where multiple threads or processes can execute instructions at the same time.\n\nIn contrast, moving a matrix over a network is slow because it involves a significant amount of data transfer between the sender and receiver."
